## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of multi-tenant isolation in cloud-native ML serving, per-tenant observability, and governance in AWS SageMaker.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant routing with PrivateLink for network isolation
- Per-tenant Feature Store namespaces for data isolation
- Canary deployments with automated rollback on drift or latency degradation
- Per-tenant monitoring, autoscaling, and governance via Model Registry

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: Route inference request to tenant-specific endpoint
function routeToTenant(req, tenantId) {
  const endpoint = tenantEndpoints.get(tenantId);
  if (!endpoint) throw new Error('Unknown tenant');

  const result = await invokeEndpoint(endpoint, req.payload);

  // Check latency and trigger rollback if needed
  if (result.latencyP99 > latencyThreshold) {
    triggerAutoRollback(tenantId);
    alertOnCallers(tenantId, 'Latency spike detected');
  }

  return result;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes designing a latency-sensitive, privacy-respecting, explainable inference service with multi-tenant isolation in AWS, plus lifecycle and cost awareness.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink, VPC, Private Data Lake, per-tenant isolation
- SageMaker endpoints, Feature Store, Model Registry
- Real-time explainability paths (Clarify/SHAP) with low latency
- Canary rollout, drift detection, monitoring and cost

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: route to appropriate prod/canary endpoint
function route(tenantId){
  const inCanary = ['tenantA','tenantB'];
  const ep = inCanary.includes(tenantId) ? 'fraud-prod-canary' : 'fraud-prod';
  return ep;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce strict per-tenant data access controls across services?
- How would you validate explainability fidelity at high throughput?
- How would you handle retraining triggers when drift is detected per tenant?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design multi-region, residency-compliant ML deployments combining real-time and batch workloads, governance, and automated rollback. Tests practical use of SageMaker Endpoint Variants, Model Registry, and drift tooling.

## Key Concepts

- Regional real-time endpoints with VPC isolation
- Per-region Feature Store governance
- Batch Transform for analytics
- Model Registry versioning
- Drift detection with Clarify
- Canary rollouts and automated rollback
- Cost controls and autoscaling

